          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em super Riemann surface
            is the analog of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            that is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branched+cover"} branched cover
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^{(1 \vert 1)}
            is canonically endowed with the structure of a super Riemann surface with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ramond+punctures"} Ramond punctures
            (
            %a{:href => "#DonagiWitten15"}> Donagi-Witten 15
            ). This implies that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adinkras"} adinkras
            encode certain very special super Riemann surfaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DoranIgaLandweberMendez-Diez13"} Doran &amp; Iga &amp; Landweber &amp; Mendez-Diez 13
          %h2#properties Properties
          %div
            %h3#NonProjectedSuperRiemannSurfaceModuli Non-projected super-moduli of super Riemann surfaces
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
              is called
              %em projected
              if it
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retraction"} retracts
              onto its bosonic
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/body"} body
            %p
              Since the computation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+scattering+amplitudes"} superstring scattering amplitudes
              involves a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berezin+integral"} Berezin integral
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} super
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
              of the given type of super Riemann surfaces, it is of interested to know when this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+super+Riemann+surfaces"} moduli space of super Riemann surfaces
              is projected, as that allows to separate the bosonic from the fermionic sectors of this “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"}> path integral
              ”.
            %p
              However, it turns out that the super-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+super+Riemann+surfaces"} moduli space of super Riemann surfaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔐
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi S
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M}_{g, n_S, n_R}
              is generically
              %em not
              projected beyond low
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              (the string’s
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+order"} loop order
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the number
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_S
                  of Neveu-punctures
              %li
                %p
                  the number
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_R
                  of Ramond-punctures.
            %p Specifically:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔐
                          %mrow
                            %mi g
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M}_{g, 0, 0}
                  is not projected for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi g
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 5
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \geq 5
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔐
                          %mrow
                            %mi g
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi n
                              %mi S
                            %mo ≥
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M}_{g, n_S \geq 1, 0}
                  is not projected for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ≥
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi S
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \geq n_S + 1
                %p
                  \&amp;lbrack;
                  %a{:href => "#DonagiWitten15"}> Donagi &amp; Witten 2015
                  \&amp;rbrack;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔐
                          %mrow
                            %mi g
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 2
                            %mi r
                            %mo ≥
                            %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M}_{g, 0, 2r \geq 2}
                  is not projected for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 5
                        %mi r
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \geq 5r + 1
                %p
                  \&amp;lbrack;
                  %a{:href => "#DonagiOtt23"}> Donagi &amp; Ott 2023
                  \&amp;rbrack;.
            %p
              On the other hand,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = 2
              (stringy
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-loop"} 2-loop
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "string+scattering+amplitude#DHokerPhong02"} D’Hoker &amp; Phong 2002
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering+amplitude"} string scattering amplitude
            %li
              %p
