            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adinkra"} adinkra
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The concept of super Riemann surfaces originates with the following articles:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Friedan"}> Daniel Friedan
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Notes On String Theory and 2-Dimensional Conformal Field Theory
            %li
              %p
                M.A. Baranov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+Schwarz"} Albert Schwarz
                %em On the Multiloop Contribution to the String Theory
                Int.J.Mod.Phys., A2:1773, 1987
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"}> Yuri Manin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Critical Dimensions of String Theories and the Dualizing Sheaf on the Moduli Space of (Super) Curves
              %p 1987
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Giddings"}> Steve Giddings
                , P. Nelson,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Geometry of super Riemann surfaces
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#DHokerPhong05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+D%27Hoker"}> Eric D'Hoker
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duong+Phong"} Duong Phong
              = succeed "," do
                %em Complex geometry and supergeometry
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cdm/1223654523"} euclid:1223654523
          %p
            Discussion of super Riemann surfaces induced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermultiplets"} supermultiplets
            for
            = succeed "-extended" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 1
            supersymmetry – via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adinkra"} adinkra
            symbols:
          %ul
            %li#DoranIgaLandweberMendez-Diez13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Doran"}> Charles Doran
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"} Kevin Iga
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Landweber"} Greg Landweber
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+M%C3%A9ndez-Diez"} Stefan Méndez-Diez
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Geometrization of
                    = succeed "-Extended" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒩
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
                %strong 19
                5 (2015) 1043-1113 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3736"}> arXiv:1311.3736
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/ATMP.2015.v19.n5.a4"} doi:10.4310/ATMP.2015.v19.n5.a4
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.charlesdoran.net/uploads/6/7/5/1/6751141/22_geometrization_of_n_extended_1_dimensional_supersymmetry_algebras_i_2015.pdf"} pdf
            %li#DoranIgaKostiukMendes-Diez16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Doran"}> Charles Doran
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"} Kevin Iga
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+M%C3%A9ndez-Diez"} Stefan Méndez-Diez
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Geometrization of
                    = succeed "-Extended" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒩
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
                %strong 22
                3 (2018) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.09983"}> arXiv:1610.09983
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesSuperModuliOfSuperRiemannSurfaces Super-Moduli space of super Riemann surfaces
            %p
              On the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+super+Riemann+surfaces"} moduli space of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Riemann+surfaces"} super Riemann surfaces
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometric
              analog of the
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+Riemann+surfaces"} moduli space of Riemann surfaces
            %ul
              %li#Rabin87
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Rabin"}> Jeffrey Rabin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Supermanifolds and Super Riemann Surfaces
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Super Field Theories
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4613-0913-0_34"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4613-0913-0_34
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/6687531"} pdf
              %li#LeBrunRothstein88
                %p
                  Claude LeBrun, Mitchell Rothstein,
